---
title: Giardiniera
cooklang: 2
servings: 12
makes: 6 pint jars
cuisine: Italian-American
source: recipe-pack snacks-sides-1/9296-giardiniera-2
---

= Vegetables -> brined vegetables

`Place` @cauliflower{400%g}(small florets), @celery{10%ribs}(diced), @carrots{5}(diced),
@red bell peppers{2}(seeded, chopped), @green olives{150%g}(sliced, pitted) and
@serrano peppers{4}(sliced) in a large #bowl{}. -> vegetables

`Pour` @kosher salt{60%g} and @-water{1.5%l} over the @&vegetables{} and `soak` for ~{6%hours}.

= Jars -> spiced jars

`Place` @dried oregano{3%tsp}, @coriander seeds{3%tsp}, @mustard seeds{1.5%tsp},
@fennel seeds{1.5%tsp}, @black peppercorns{1.5%tsp}, @?red chili flakes{1.5%tsp}(for hot jars),
@celery seeds{3/4%tsp} and @bay leaves{6} divided among six #pint jars{6}.

`Drain` the @&brined vegetables{} and `rinse` them in a #colander{}, then `pack` the
@&brined vegetables{} into the #&pint jars{} with @garlic{6%cloves}(halved).

= Brine -> brine

`Bring` @water{1%l}, @white wine vinegar{1%l} and @&kosher salt{2%tbsp} to a boil in a
#saucepan{}.

= Fill and store -> giardiniera

`Pour` the boiling @&brine{} into the #&pint jars{}, leaving 1.5 cm of headspace, and `top` each
jar with @extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp}.

`Wipe` the rims with a wet #paper towel{} and `seal` the jars.

`Rest` at room temperature for ~rest{1-2%days}, then `refrigerate` for at least ~chill{2-3%days}
before eating.
